00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:40.690
SPEAKER 4: A reading
of the 19th Psalm.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.300
"The heavens declare
the glory of God.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.970
And the firmament
shows his handiwork.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.020
One day speaks to another.

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.680
And one night gives
knowledge to another.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.020
There is neither
speech nor language.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.210
And their voices are not heard.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.250
But their sound has gone
out into all the lands

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.980
and their words to
the end of the world.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:04.240
In them, he has set a
tent for the sun, which

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:08.170
comes forth as a bridegroom
out of his chamber and rejoices

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:11.430
like a strong man
to run his course.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.660
It goes forth from the uttermost
parts of the heavens and runs

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.800
about to the end of it again.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.730
And there is nothing
hidden from its heat.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.330
The law of the Lord is
perfect, reviving the soul.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.790
The testimony of
the Lord is sure

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.080
and gives wisdom to the simple.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:32.420
The statutes of the Lord are
right and rejoice the heart.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.700
The commandment of
the Lord is pure

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.950
and gives light to the eyes.

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:40.880
The fear of the Lord is
clean and endures forever.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.930
The judgments of the Lord are
true and righteous altogether,

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:47.390
more to be desired
are they than gold,

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.870
even much find gold,
sweeter also than honey,

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.360
than the drippings
from the honeycomb.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:55.970
Moreover, by them is
your servant taught.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:59.120
And in keeping them,
there is great reward.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:02.000
Who can tell how
often he offends?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.000
O cleanse me from
my secret faults.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.850
Keep your servant also from
presumptuous ends, lest they

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:09.990
get the dominion over me.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:14.210
So shall I be undefiled, an
innocent of great offense.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:17.630
Let the words of my mouth and
the meditation of my heart

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:20.870
be always acceptable in
your sight, O Lord, my rock

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.820
and my redeemer."

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.850
Glory be to the
Father and to the Son

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:29.570
and to the Holy Spirit, as
it was in the beginning,

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:34.250
is now, and ever shall be,
world without end, Amen.

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:54.420
SPEAKER 5: Here
begins the 11th verse

00:14:54.420 --> 00:15:00.110
of the second chapter of St.
Paul's letter to the Ephesians.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.590
"Therefore, remember
that at one time

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:07.310
you Gentiles in the flesh called
'the uncircumcision' by what

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:10.400
is called the circumcision,
which is made in the flesh

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.900
by hands.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:15.050
Remember that you
were at that time

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:19.130
separated from Christ,
alienated from the commonwealth

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:23.780
of Israel, and strangers the
covenants of promise, having

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:27.590
no hope and without
God in the world.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:32.150
But now, in Christ Jesus,
you who once were far off

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:35.630
have been brought nearby
the blood of Christ.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:40.340
For He himself is our peace,
who has made us both one

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:44.420
and has broken down in his flesh
the dividing wall of hostility

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.940
by abolishing the law of
commandments expressed

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:51.650
in ordinances that He
might create in himself one

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:56.350
new man in place of the
two, so making peace,

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.480
and might reconcile
us both to God and one

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:03.150
body through the cross,
thereby killing the hostility.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:03.900
And he came.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.840
And He preached peace to
you were far off and peace

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:08.760
to those who were near.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.690
For through Him,
we both have access

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.260
in one spirit to the Father.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:17.880
So then you are no longer
strangers and aliens,

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.780
but you are fellow citizens
with the saints and members

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.150
of the household of God.

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:27.720
Built on the foundation of
the apostles and prophets,

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.450
Christ Jesus himself
being the cornerstone

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:33.810
in whom the whole structure,
being joined together,

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:37.710
grows into a holy
temple in the Lord.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:42.060
In Him you also are being
built together into a dwelling

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.960
place for God by the spirit."

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:46.920
Here ends the lesson.

00:17:40.812 --> 00:17:44.804
CHOIR: (SINGING) [INAUDIBLE]

00:24:45.368 --> 00:24:49.490
LARRY ARNN: The Psalmist
writes, "Unless the Lord

00:24:49.490 --> 00:24:54.450
builds the house, those who
build it labor in vain."

00:24:54.450 --> 00:24:56.630
A lesser authority,
but still an authority,

00:24:56.630 --> 00:25:00.450
Winston Churchill writes,
"We shape our buildings.

00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:02.280
And afterwards, they shape us."

00:25:07.720 --> 00:25:10.390
We have cause to think that this
is the largest classical chapel

00:25:10.390 --> 00:25:12.930
built in 70 years.

00:25:12.930 --> 00:25:16.920
It's hard to prove a negative,
but the one we can find

00:25:16.920 --> 00:25:20.160
is the Marsh Chapel at
Boston University, which

00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:28.360
was begun in 1920 and
finished in 1950, 70 years.

00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:33.810
The question is not
why we built this.

00:25:33.810 --> 00:25:36.660
Does it call out to you?

00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:39.450
When you walk in here,
don't you look up and think

00:25:39.450 --> 00:25:42.140
of the ultimate things?

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:43.940
The answer to that
question is obvious.

00:25:43.940 --> 00:25:49.260
The hard question is,
why have others not?

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.253
It's not expense.

00:25:51.253 --> 00:25:53.670
More expensive buildings--
this is an expensive building--

00:25:53.670 --> 00:25:56.070
more expensive buildings than
this are built every year

00:25:56.070 --> 00:25:58.910
on college campuses.

00:25:58.910 --> 00:26:00.430
It's not lack of example.

00:26:00.430 --> 00:26:04.240
Any old college
campus, or almost any,

00:26:04.240 --> 00:26:07.660
has buildings like
this to look at.

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:10.990
Why do they not emulate them?

00:26:10.990 --> 00:26:15.210
That would need to be some
powerful cause, something

00:26:15.210 --> 00:26:16.410
to obstruct that.

00:26:22.610 --> 00:26:25.530
I think it is the
most powerful cause.

00:26:25.530 --> 00:26:31.460
I think it is a turning away
from things that are beautiful,

00:26:31.460 --> 00:26:35.388
which means necessarily then
also things that are true

00:26:35.388 --> 00:26:36.430
and things that are good.

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:43.290
When the truth and the
beauty and good are gone,

00:26:43.290 --> 00:26:45.390
then, of course all
reasons that demand

00:26:45.390 --> 00:26:50.010
we strive to become good
human beings are gone.

00:26:50.010 --> 00:26:53.160
And those reasons, disappear the
justification and requirement

00:26:53.160 --> 00:26:56.440
for human freedom.

00:26:56.440 --> 00:26:59.590
Also go all the
precepts that guide us

00:26:59.590 --> 00:27:01.780
to the use of our freedom
towards civilization.

00:27:05.020 --> 00:27:08.280
It is as if a plague
has come over the land

00:27:08.280 --> 00:27:10.640
and that plague has
destroyed many colleges.

00:27:10.640 --> 00:27:12.590
And if it proceeds
to its culmination,

00:27:12.590 --> 00:27:15.208
it will destroy this one too.

00:27:15.208 --> 00:27:16.250
But that will not happen.

00:27:20.560 --> 00:27:25.260
We can't really today explain
all of that that I just said.

00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:27.930
It is actually the purpose of
the activity of the college

00:27:27.930 --> 00:27:30.380
to explain and
understand all that.

00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:36.480
And that activity goes on
intensely now for 175 years.

00:27:36.480 --> 00:27:41.080
What we can do is say
what caused this building.

00:27:41.080 --> 00:27:42.480
It was caused by several things.

00:27:45.220 --> 00:27:50.500
It is made of matter, stone and
steel, plaster and wood, glass,

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:52.170
and granite.

00:27:52.170 --> 00:27:54.550
The marble in 12
varieties comes from--

00:27:54.550 --> 00:27:56.710
and some rose onyx--

00:27:56.710 --> 00:28:00.700
comes from Carrera
in Italy where

00:28:00.700 --> 00:28:06.280
they are quarrying to repair
the cathedral of Milan.

00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:09.050
The limestone is from
quarries in Indiana

00:28:09.050 --> 00:28:12.650
that supplied most of
the limestone that's

00:28:12.650 --> 00:28:14.930
in the nation's capital, in
those great old classical

00:28:14.930 --> 00:28:17.020
buildings.

00:28:17.020 --> 00:28:20.780
The granite come from Georgia,
Vermont, and Missouri.

00:28:20.780 --> 00:28:23.480
The silver cloud granite
on the fountain outside

00:28:23.480 --> 00:28:25.760
comes from India.

00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:30.080
The brass cross up
here is from Spain.

00:28:30.080 --> 00:28:31.610
We like to publish
that old essay

00:28:31.610 --> 00:28:35.530
by Leonard Read, "I, a Pencil."

00:28:35.530 --> 00:28:37.210
And that's the
strongest demonstration

00:28:37.210 --> 00:28:39.820
I've ever read of the utter
power of the free market.

00:28:39.820 --> 00:28:42.010
Because, actually,
this building has

00:28:42.010 --> 00:28:43.930
been produced by the
cooperation of people

00:28:43.930 --> 00:28:47.638
all over the world who
don't know each other,

00:28:47.638 --> 00:28:49.680
often didn't know what
they were contributing to.

00:28:53.890 --> 00:28:57.540
This building has
been built by people.

00:28:57.540 --> 00:28:59.370
Begin with the
designer, the architect.

00:29:02.510 --> 00:29:05.240
Aristotle speaks of art
that are architectonic.

00:29:05.240 --> 00:29:07.070
It comes from the
combination of arca--

00:29:07.070 --> 00:29:09.830
beginning or rule or principle--

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:12.210
and techne, art.

00:29:12.210 --> 00:29:14.780
It's the art that commands.

00:29:14.780 --> 00:29:16.920
It organizes all
the things under it.

00:29:19.900 --> 00:29:21.700
Abstracted from
its chief meaning

00:29:21.700 --> 00:29:27.305
in the design of buildings,
it just means ruling, art.

00:29:27.305 --> 00:29:29.290
Our architect is
and is understood

00:29:29.290 --> 00:29:32.320
to be one of the
best in the world.

00:29:32.320 --> 00:29:34.360
He is Duncan Stroik.

00:29:34.360 --> 00:29:36.220
He was assisted
mostly by many people,

00:29:36.220 --> 00:29:39.460
but mostly by Tom Stroka
and Jamie LaCourt.

00:29:43.170 --> 00:29:45.240
His credentials are sterling.

00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:46.810
He went to Yale and Harvard.

00:29:46.810 --> 00:29:47.950
No, he went to--

00:29:47.950 --> 00:29:48.690
where'd you go?

00:29:48.690 --> 00:29:49.990
Where did he go?

00:29:49.990 --> 00:29:51.340
It doesn't matter where he went.

00:29:51.340 --> 00:29:52.680
He went to Virginia and Yale.

00:29:57.440 --> 00:30:00.640
He says his teachers are
Thomas Jefferson and others.

00:30:00.640 --> 00:30:03.500
But his direct teacher
was Allan Greenberg

00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:05.440
who's one of the
midwives the revival

00:30:05.440 --> 00:30:09.310
of classical architecture in
our time, a very great man.

00:30:13.220 --> 00:30:15.377
Duncan can stand
for all the artisans

00:30:15.377 --> 00:30:17.210
who've worked on this
because he's the first

00:30:17.210 --> 00:30:19.070
and he commanded the others.

00:30:19.070 --> 00:30:22.546
I'd like Duncan and his
colleagues to stand up, please.

00:30:22.546 --> 00:30:26.032
[APPLAUSE]

00:30:44.937 --> 00:30:46.020
That caused me to look up.

00:30:46.020 --> 00:30:48.520
And it leads me to remind you
kids sitting on the front row,

00:30:48.520 --> 00:30:50.622
don't fall off.

00:30:50.622 --> 00:30:52.080
Duncan and I are
having an argument

00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:55.240
about whether those
rails are too low.

00:30:55.240 --> 00:30:56.160
So far he wins.

00:31:00.220 --> 00:31:04.960
The fountain outside was
designed by another architect.

00:31:04.960 --> 00:31:06.940
Her name is Alice Arnn.

00:31:06.940 --> 00:31:09.862
And she might stand up, please.

00:31:09.862 --> 00:31:13.334
[APPLAUSE]

00:31:23.260 --> 00:31:24.400
I happen to know that girl.

00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:26.410
And she will not like it
that I made her stand up.

00:31:26.410 --> 00:31:27.820
And she really
would not like if I

00:31:27.820 --> 00:31:29.945
didn't mention that Duncan
Stroik helped her a lot.

00:31:37.960 --> 00:31:40.781
The builders built
this building.

00:31:40.781 --> 00:31:44.070
They're Weigand Construction.

00:31:44.070 --> 00:31:46.640
They work for us a lot.

00:31:46.640 --> 00:31:48.950
They're awesome.

00:31:48.950 --> 00:31:51.560
They're losing money on this.

00:31:51.560 --> 00:31:55.090
They would be one of the
biggest contributors to this.

00:31:55.090 --> 00:31:58.990
They estimated, with their
usual precision and skill--

00:31:58.990 --> 00:32:01.810
but nobody's done
this in living memory,

00:32:01.810 --> 00:32:04.770
there's no one alive
who's done this.

00:32:04.770 --> 00:32:06.723
And so they got
some things wrong.

00:32:06.723 --> 00:32:08.140
And those happen
to be things that

00:32:08.140 --> 00:32:12.070
are in their responsibility.

00:32:12.070 --> 00:32:14.200
They told us about it.

00:32:14.200 --> 00:32:16.180
They asked us not
to tell the workmen

00:32:16.180 --> 00:32:22.000
because they didn't want the
workmen to change anything.

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.667
Then they mentioned
that maybe they'd

00:32:23.667 --> 00:32:25.500
hope to work for the
college again sometime.

00:32:25.500 --> 00:32:29.280
And we told them that that
would have happened anyway.

00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:34.500
The workmen on the
building, we're

00:32:34.500 --> 00:32:36.875
going to have a convocation
soon in here for the college.

00:32:36.875 --> 00:32:38.625
And we're going to
invite all the workmen.

00:32:38.625 --> 00:32:41.430
And we're going to put a plaque
up, put their names on it here.

00:32:41.430 --> 00:32:44.850
And I will tell you that
they work into the night.

00:32:44.850 --> 00:32:47.070
Mark, the supervisor,
told me that he'd not

00:32:47.070 --> 00:32:50.130
been to his beloved
lake for two years.

00:32:50.130 --> 00:32:55.840
There were 60 people working
here on Tuesday of this week.

00:32:55.840 --> 00:32:57.990
And I never see them stop work.

00:32:57.990 --> 00:33:00.360
Except I come in
and they come to see

00:33:00.360 --> 00:33:03.020
me and they want to
show me something.

00:33:03.020 --> 00:33:05.468
And they thank me
for the privilege

00:33:05.468 --> 00:33:06.510
of helping to build this.

00:33:09.480 --> 00:33:10.950
They made this building.

00:33:14.150 --> 00:33:18.020
My colleagues have made this
building, working together

00:33:18.020 --> 00:33:21.170
for 20 years now,
which Pewe has taken

00:33:21.170 --> 00:33:25.020
the lead in doing all of this.

00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:27.030
And so, of course,
it's his responsibility

00:33:27.030 --> 00:33:30.522
that the east arcade
is not quite finished.

00:33:30.522 --> 00:33:33.490
[LAUGHTER]

00:33:33.490 --> 00:33:38.470
John Sweeney's hand is in
everything here on the campus.

00:33:38.470 --> 00:33:41.080
The way we work together,
David Whalen, Diane Philipp,

00:33:41.080 --> 00:33:44.920
Mike Harner, several others,
we sat for hours with Duncan.

00:33:44.920 --> 00:33:47.200
They were delightful hours too.

00:33:47.200 --> 00:33:52.300
Duncan is very quick and
intelligent and also stubborn.

00:33:52.300 --> 00:33:57.098
And the plan emerged
from those meetings.

00:33:57.098 --> 00:33:59.140
And the building would be
different without them.

00:34:03.170 --> 00:34:07.440
All of you built this building.

00:34:07.440 --> 00:34:11.110
Begin with Jack and Jo Babbitt.

00:34:11.110 --> 00:34:16.989
Jo said to me in an providential
and embarrassing thing,

00:34:16.989 --> 00:34:20.780
she saw that little chapel that
she calls a wine cellar now

00:34:20.780 --> 00:34:23.420
that was serving
as a chapel here.

00:34:23.420 --> 00:34:25.420
The college has always
had a chapel, by the way.

00:34:25.420 --> 00:34:28.449
There used to be one up in
the top of Central Hall.

00:34:28.449 --> 00:34:30.250
It was quite pretty back then.

00:34:30.250 --> 00:34:35.949
And we built the College
Baptist Church in the 1870s.

00:34:35.949 --> 00:34:40.578
But we didn't have any
chapel on the campus,

00:34:40.578 --> 00:34:41.620
except that little thing.

00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:43.245
And she just thought
that was terrible.

00:34:43.245 --> 00:34:46.528
And she said, "Why don't
you have a proper chapel?"

00:34:46.528 --> 00:34:48.070
And I said, "Well,
I've been waiting.

00:34:48.070 --> 00:34:49.370
We have a plan for one."

00:34:49.370 --> 00:34:51.610
We made a plan for
the campus in 2001

00:34:51.610 --> 00:34:55.170
and there's a
chapel on the plan.

00:34:55.170 --> 00:34:57.700
And I said, "I've been
waiting for somebody to say,

00:34:57.700 --> 00:35:01.440
'you need an excellent chapel,
I would like to help you build

00:35:01.440 --> 00:35:02.640
that.'"

00:35:02.640 --> 00:35:06.490
And she repeated those
words back to me.

00:35:06.490 --> 00:35:08.530
Think of what that means.

00:35:08.530 --> 00:35:10.400
Her name is back there.

00:35:10.400 --> 00:35:14.110
We had to fight to
get that and Jack's.

00:35:14.110 --> 00:35:17.320
But Christ Chapel,
she wanted it to be

00:35:17.320 --> 00:35:22.390
called, which is, of course,
exactly the right thing.

00:35:22.390 --> 00:35:24.722
Jack and Jo, stand up please.

00:35:24.722 --> 00:35:28.194
[APPLAUSE]

00:36:04.950 --> 00:36:07.690
You'll see some other names on
one of the plaques out there.

00:36:07.690 --> 00:36:09.857
There's not that many
recognitions in this building.

00:36:09.857 --> 00:36:11.130
Most people didn't want it.

00:36:11.130 --> 00:36:13.680
But Bill Atherton and his
family are right there.

00:36:13.680 --> 00:36:19.416
And people have been
so generous, you know?

00:36:19.416 --> 00:36:22.310
And why do they do that?

00:36:22.310 --> 00:36:25.710
Same reason we do
what we do here.

00:36:25.710 --> 00:36:28.080
That makes, by the
way, all of you,

00:36:28.080 --> 00:36:32.430
that makes everyone who will see
the ceremony, everyone who will

00:36:32.430 --> 00:36:34.170
take joy from this chapel--

00:36:34.170 --> 00:36:36.810
and that will be millions--

00:36:36.810 --> 00:36:39.860
it means that they
are here today.

00:36:39.860 --> 00:36:44.215
And they are among the
builders of this building.

00:36:44.215 --> 00:36:48.550
The faculty and the
students are crucial because

00:36:48.550 --> 00:36:50.560
without the activities
that they carry on,

00:36:50.560 --> 00:36:54.002
I argue better than
anywhere on Earth,

00:36:54.002 --> 00:36:55.460
how would anybody
think that it was

00:36:55.460 --> 00:36:59.160
even plausible that we could
have a building like this?

00:36:59.160 --> 00:37:03.642
And yet, because of them
and their work, they fit.

00:37:03.642 --> 00:37:04.660
I thank you all.

00:37:07.840 --> 00:37:12.970
Even those kids up there, who
I do hope they don't fall off,

00:37:12.970 --> 00:37:15.148
but if they do, we can get more.

00:37:15.148 --> 00:37:18.136
[LAUGHTER]

00:37:30.590 --> 00:37:33.190
This building has a form.

00:37:33.190 --> 00:37:36.550
It is classical.

00:37:36.550 --> 00:37:37.410
What does that mean?

00:37:37.410 --> 00:37:40.850
Does that mean that it
looks Greek or Roman?

00:37:40.850 --> 00:37:45.080
It turns out that the innovation
of the Greeks and the Romans

00:37:45.080 --> 00:37:46.730
was to look beyond
their own things

00:37:46.730 --> 00:37:51.110
to the things that are
right, whatever their source

00:37:51.110 --> 00:37:54.228
or place of origin.

00:37:54.228 --> 00:37:55.270
That's not what it means.

00:37:58.090 --> 00:38:00.340
Unlike Duncan Stroik
and my daughter,

00:38:00.340 --> 00:38:02.830
I've actually paid tuition
at an architecture school.

00:38:09.070 --> 00:38:14.486
And I feel entitled to
speak on the subject.

00:38:14.486 --> 00:38:21.100
[LAUGHTER]

00:38:21.100 --> 00:38:24.190
Classical architecture,
I've teased it out of them.

00:38:24.190 --> 00:38:26.530
They don't, by the way, they're
reticent about revealing

00:38:26.530 --> 00:38:28.120
their secrets.

00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:30.790
They want you to think it's all
just a mystery, because it is.

00:38:30.790 --> 00:38:33.460
But they're like--
especially Alice,

00:38:33.460 --> 00:38:34.870
she's much worse than Duncan.

00:38:38.060 --> 00:38:40.970
It has to fit in its place.

00:38:40.970 --> 00:38:44.650
It has to go with the
things that are around it.

00:38:44.650 --> 00:38:50.620
We have a beautiful building
right over there, 1852.

00:38:50.620 --> 00:38:53.710
Some of the most important
things in American history

00:38:53.710 --> 00:38:55.370
have happened in there.

00:38:55.370 --> 00:38:57.370
Frederick Douglass
spoke in there.

00:39:00.040 --> 00:39:03.490
The building points up.

00:39:03.490 --> 00:39:05.350
The ceilings are high.

00:39:05.350 --> 00:39:12.530
The windows are generous,
arched at the top like this.

00:39:12.530 --> 00:39:14.890
This has to fit with that.

00:39:14.890 --> 00:39:17.550
One of Duncan's
inventions, because he

00:39:17.550 --> 00:39:18.960
knew all that in a heartbeat.

00:39:18.960 --> 00:39:21.920
In fact, he showed us pictures
of some of the new buildings

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:22.920
because he didn't know--

00:39:22.920 --> 00:39:24.930
either he's more artful
even than I think

00:39:24.930 --> 00:39:27.407
or he didn't know
that they were new.

00:39:27.407 --> 00:39:29.490
And he said, boy, people
who planned this college,

00:39:29.490 --> 00:39:32.550
they really thought hard about
how to make it work altogether.

00:39:32.550 --> 00:39:35.190
You have to live up to
that responsibility.

00:39:35.190 --> 00:39:37.167
And later Whalen pointed
out to him, I think,

00:39:37.167 --> 00:39:39.000
that he was talking
about two buildings that

00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:39.930
were six years old.

00:39:42.303 --> 00:39:43.720
We were a little
cocky about that.

00:39:47.160 --> 00:39:50.700
But it has two towers.

00:39:50.700 --> 00:39:52.830
Because if it just
had one, it would

00:39:52.830 --> 00:39:56.650
have to be much higher
than Central Hall.

00:39:56.650 --> 00:39:58.220
And that would not be right.

00:39:58.220 --> 00:40:01.630
So although it's much
larger than Central Hall,

00:40:01.630 --> 00:40:05.080
it fits here in its place.

00:40:05.080 --> 00:40:08.360
The materials have to work.

00:40:08.360 --> 00:40:13.250
This is a yellow brick,
the old thing here.

00:40:13.250 --> 00:40:15.890
I confess, I did have a woman
say to me one time looking

00:40:15.890 --> 00:40:17.990
at Strosacker Hall
after we remodeled

00:40:17.990 --> 00:40:21.210
it, she said, "Dr. Arnn,
is that a green building?"

00:40:21.210 --> 00:40:22.370
And I said, "No, ma'am.

00:40:22.370 --> 00:40:24.874
That building is yellow."

00:40:24.874 --> 00:40:33.010
[LAUGHTER]

00:40:33.010 --> 00:40:36.392
That lady was a donor.

00:40:36.392 --> 00:40:37.600
I don't know if she still is.

00:40:42.930 --> 00:40:45.360
It means more than
proportion even.

00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:50.750
It means it's right, whatever it
is that takes to make it right.

00:40:50.750 --> 00:40:53.350
It has to be like that.

00:40:53.350 --> 00:40:55.760
It's a classical building.

00:40:55.760 --> 00:40:58.320
It's like what the Greeks did.

00:40:58.320 --> 00:41:00.920
A blessing to all of us, we
study that here, of course.

00:41:07.535 --> 00:41:09.160
I have one more cause
to name, but I'll

00:41:09.160 --> 00:41:12.370
name it at the moment we
dedicate the building.

00:41:12.370 --> 00:41:15.310
Right now, I will say that
the ceremony would not

00:41:15.310 --> 00:41:18.610
be right if there were not
the right kind of speaker.

00:41:21.665 --> 00:41:23.040
I don't know that
I know another.

00:41:26.120 --> 00:41:28.080
We were talking about
how we would do this.

00:41:28.080 --> 00:41:29.455
And I said, you
know, the college

00:41:29.455 --> 00:41:31.700
stands for these four things.

00:41:31.700 --> 00:41:35.920
We're going to need somebody who
represents these four things.

00:41:35.920 --> 00:41:39.520
Somebody has to
have a character--

00:41:39.520 --> 00:41:43.195
self-effacing,
courageous, assertive.

00:41:46.660 --> 00:41:49.550
Somebody has to have learning.

00:41:49.550 --> 00:41:51.830
Do you know what
he's accomplishing?

00:41:51.830 --> 00:41:53.700
It's breathtaking.

00:41:53.700 --> 00:41:55.850
I knew him before
he got on the court.

00:41:55.850 --> 00:41:58.420
And I once thanked him for this.

00:41:58.420 --> 00:42:02.230
Because what he's doing is, in
the ordinary doing of his work,

00:42:02.230 --> 00:42:07.300
in his joining in verdicts and
his explaining his opinion,

00:42:07.300 --> 00:42:10.810
he is writing an accurate
constitutional history

00:42:10.810 --> 00:42:12.910
of the United States.

00:42:12.910 --> 00:42:16.930
And he's showing a way
out of the distortions

00:42:16.930 --> 00:42:21.420
that have come upon us for
the last three generations.

00:42:21.420 --> 00:42:23.100
It is breathtaking.

00:42:23.100 --> 00:42:27.270
If you doubt it, read three
opinions, my favorite,

00:42:27.270 --> 00:42:33.090
US versus Lopez, Missouri
versus Jenkins, and the recent,

00:42:33.090 --> 00:42:35.920
McDonald versus Chicago.

00:42:35.920 --> 00:42:40.580
And they show the
way to fix all this

00:42:40.580 --> 00:42:43.750
so far as the court can fix it.

00:42:43.750 --> 00:42:48.870
A learned man, it
would have to be

00:42:48.870 --> 00:42:51.690
a man who loves freedom and
the American constitutional

00:42:51.690 --> 00:42:54.090
republic.

00:42:54.090 --> 00:42:59.120
This man is the greatest living
interpreter of those things.

00:42:59.120 --> 00:43:03.710
And finally, it would have to
be a man of faith, somebody who

00:43:03.710 --> 00:43:05.670
bows in humility before God.

00:43:08.580 --> 00:43:11.540
Think of those things together.

00:43:11.540 --> 00:43:15.700
Who would be like that?

00:43:15.700 --> 00:43:17.100
Clarence Thomas.

00:43:17.100 --> 00:43:21.972
[APPLAUSE]

00:43:37.813 --> 00:43:38.938
CLARENCE THOMAS: Thank you.

00:43:42.431 --> 00:43:43.429
Thank you.

00:43:51.912 --> 00:43:54.548
I feel like quitting
while I'm ahead.

00:43:54.548 --> 00:43:56.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:43:56.300 --> 00:43:58.810
Thank you, Dr. Arnn.

00:43:58.810 --> 00:44:02.950
And thank you for
inviting my wife and me

00:44:02.950 --> 00:44:06.040
to Hillsdale once again.

00:44:06.040 --> 00:44:11.470
It seems like homecoming,
we've been here so often.

00:44:11.470 --> 00:44:14.600
The campus is magnificent.

00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:20.860
I'm honored to have
this task of speaking

00:44:20.860 --> 00:44:22.910
to you all this afternoon--

00:44:22.910 --> 00:44:23.970
or this morning.

00:44:28.090 --> 00:44:31.570
But I wondered as
Dr. Arnn was speaking

00:44:31.570 --> 00:44:33.590
whether I'm up to that task.

00:44:33.590 --> 00:44:36.660
And I pray that I am.

00:44:36.660 --> 00:44:38.980
This is a very special occasion.

00:44:38.980 --> 00:44:44.960
It's the 175th
anniversary of Hillsdale

00:44:44.960 --> 00:44:47.285
and the dedication of
this beautiful chapel.

00:44:50.610 --> 00:44:56.070
Christ Chapel is a culmination
of years of generosity,

00:44:56.070 --> 00:44:58.290
planning, and hard work.

00:45:00.860 --> 00:45:07.450
And the end result is at
once stunning and glorious.

00:45:07.450 --> 00:45:12.190
The chapel's enduring beauty
highlights the transcendence,

00:45:12.190 --> 00:45:17.060
the sovereignty, and
the grace of God.

00:45:17.060 --> 00:45:21.410
It truly illustrates
how architectural design

00:45:21.410 --> 00:45:26.450
can reflect the character of God
and evoke a sense of reverence

00:45:26.450 --> 00:45:27.125
for his majesty.

00:45:29.820 --> 00:45:35.490
Everyone involved in
the financing, planning,

00:45:35.490 --> 00:45:41.140
and the construction of this
chapel should rightly be proud.

00:45:41.140 --> 00:45:46.420
It is a magnificent
accomplishment.

00:45:46.420 --> 00:45:49.130
But we have gathered
here today not just

00:45:49.130 --> 00:45:50.765
to admire this beautiful chapel.

00:45:53.750 --> 00:45:58.010
We are also here to dedicate it.

00:45:58.010 --> 00:46:01.040
The word dedicate
in this context

00:46:01.040 --> 00:46:06.560
means to set apart and
consecrate to a deity

00:46:06.560 --> 00:46:10.280
or to a sacred purpose.

00:46:10.280 --> 00:46:14.490
To appropriately dedicate
this chapel then,

00:46:14.490 --> 00:46:21.180
it is worthwhile to reflect
on the purposes for which we

00:46:21.180 --> 00:46:25.020
are here, we are setting
apart this sacred place

00:46:25.020 --> 00:46:26.025
on a college campus.

00:46:29.110 --> 00:46:32.590
The primary purpose
of a chapel is

00:46:32.590 --> 00:46:37.790
to provide a place where man
can enter the presence of God.

00:46:37.790 --> 00:46:40.520
It provides a
sanctuary in which man

00:46:40.520 --> 00:46:44.810
can withdraw from the
chaos of our world

00:46:44.810 --> 00:46:49.010
and seek a sacred stillness.

00:46:49.010 --> 00:46:53.480
For as Elijah learned
on Mount Horeb,

00:46:53.480 --> 00:46:58.520
God so often comes to
us not in the storms,

00:46:58.520 --> 00:47:04.180
not in the earthquakes or fires
of life, but in stillness,

00:47:04.180 --> 00:47:07.450
in a gentle whisper.

00:47:07.450 --> 00:47:12.610
Accordingly, men and women
have long sought respite

00:47:12.610 --> 00:47:16.930
from the noise and
commotion of daily life,

00:47:16.930 --> 00:47:20.080
where they can be
still and know that he

00:47:20.080 --> 00:47:25.330
is God, where they
can seek an inner calm

00:47:25.330 --> 00:47:28.790
and a transcendent peace.

00:47:28.790 --> 00:47:32.170
Beautiful chapels
such as this one

00:47:32.170 --> 00:47:36.250
provide that sacred
space for stillness,

00:47:36.250 --> 00:47:40.850
a place for an encounter
with the divine.

00:47:40.850 --> 00:47:42.710
As the architect
of this chapel has

00:47:42.710 --> 00:47:46.440
written, when you
enter a church,

00:47:46.440 --> 00:47:50.130
it is as if you are
entering through a gateway

00:47:50.130 --> 00:47:52.245
from the profane
toward the sacred.

00:47:54.880 --> 00:48:00.130
It is difficult to overstate
the significance of the role

00:48:00.130 --> 00:48:04.160
that this particular chapel will
play in the life of Hillsdale

00:48:04.160 --> 00:48:04.660
College.

00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:13.210
Many of life's momentous
events take place in chapels.

00:48:13.210 --> 00:48:16.370
Take weddings for example.

00:48:16.370 --> 00:48:22.010
When a couple enters into the
sacred covenant of marriage,

00:48:22.010 --> 00:48:26.420
they do so not only
before friends and family,

00:48:26.420 --> 00:48:30.430
but also before almighty God.

00:48:30.430 --> 00:48:33.340
When the wedding is
held in the chapel,

00:48:33.340 --> 00:48:37.240
the chapel exalts the
occasion and signifies

00:48:37.240 --> 00:48:43.950
that God himself is a witness to
the couples' exchange of vows.

00:48:43.950 --> 00:48:48.690
Or reflect on funerals
and memorial services.

00:48:48.690 --> 00:48:52.770
As we grieve the loss of a
friend or a family member

00:48:52.770 --> 00:48:55.680
and reflect on
their lives, we also

00:48:55.680 --> 00:49:00.540
seek comfort, hope, and peace.

00:49:00.540 --> 00:49:04.290
Conducting that solemn
service in a chapel

00:49:04.290 --> 00:49:06.450
reminds us that
our deepest needs

00:49:06.450 --> 00:49:11.050
are met through God, who is
near to the brokenhearted,

00:49:11.050 --> 00:49:14.490
the wretched, and the lonely.

00:49:14.490 --> 00:49:18.660
And as we are drawn to
reflect on that eternal life

00:49:18.660 --> 00:49:24.250
beyond the grave, a sacred
space, such as this chapel,

00:49:24.250 --> 00:49:28.660
with an image of the cross,
that old rugged cross,

00:49:28.660 --> 00:49:32.140
serves as a poignant
testament to the hope

00:49:32.140 --> 00:49:34.890
of the resurrection.

00:49:34.890 --> 00:49:39.510
Chapels also provide a space
for other important activities

00:49:39.510 --> 00:49:43.170
that take place on a
more regular basis.

00:49:43.170 --> 00:49:48.090
For example, worship services
will be held in this chapel.

00:49:48.090 --> 00:49:51.450
If our highest purpose
is to glorify God,

00:49:51.450 --> 00:49:55.350
what better resource to
provide on a college campus

00:49:55.350 --> 00:49:58.990
than a chapel that
allows students, faculty,

00:49:58.990 --> 00:50:03.300
administrators, staff, and
visitors to gather together

00:50:03.300 --> 00:50:04.690
for worship and prayer?

00:50:08.560 --> 00:50:12.490
This chapel also will serve
as a setting for ceremonies

00:50:12.490 --> 00:50:15.890
and liturgical
concerts, allowing

00:50:15.890 --> 00:50:19.550
all who gather here to
learn together and celebrate

00:50:19.550 --> 00:50:21.860
before God.

00:50:21.860 --> 00:50:27.320
And the chapel will
be used regularly

00:50:27.320 --> 00:50:31.580
for personal prayers of
reflection, meditation,

00:50:31.580 --> 00:50:34.670
confession, repentance,
forgiveness,

00:50:34.670 --> 00:50:37.700
and reconciliation.

00:50:37.700 --> 00:50:41.120
Chapels are particularly
important in providing a place

00:50:41.120 --> 00:50:46.890
for the burdened, for the
brokenhearted and despairing.

00:50:46.890 --> 00:50:49.980
When life is difficult
and seems pointless,

00:50:49.980 --> 00:50:53.700
we need a safe haven where
we can escape from the storm

00:50:53.700 --> 00:50:55.860
and find solace.

00:50:55.860 --> 00:50:58.910
Chapels provide that setting.

00:50:58.910 --> 00:51:01.670
They invite us to
draw near to God

00:51:01.670 --> 00:51:05.510
and to elevate our thoughts,
to seek his wisdom,

00:51:05.510 --> 00:51:09.560
to lay down our burdens
at the foot of the cross,

00:51:09.560 --> 00:51:15.150
and to find that peace that
surpasses all understanding.

00:51:15.150 --> 00:51:20.350
For here we know we are
standing on holy ground.

00:51:20.350 --> 00:51:23.530
In the words of a
popular gospel hymn,

00:51:23.530 --> 00:51:27.340
"When I walk through the
door, I sense His presence.

00:51:27.340 --> 00:51:32.140
And I knew this place, this
was a place where love abounds,

00:51:32.140 --> 00:51:33.930
for this is a temple.

00:51:33.930 --> 00:51:36.560
The God we love abides here.

00:51:36.560 --> 00:51:40.750
Oh, we are standing in the
presence, his presence,

00:51:40.750 --> 00:51:41.640
on holy ground."

00:51:47.420 --> 00:51:53.240
This calls to mind Hannah, the
mother of the prophet Samuel.

00:51:53.240 --> 00:51:56.630
When she came to the
tabernacle to pray,

00:51:56.630 --> 00:52:00.640
she was barren but
longed for a child.

00:52:00.640 --> 00:52:05.620
The Bible describes her
as deeply depressed,

00:52:05.620 --> 00:52:08.800
a woman troubled
in spirit who was

00:52:08.800 --> 00:52:15.850
experiencing great anxiety and
vexation, and weeping bitterly.

00:52:15.850 --> 00:52:19.510
But Hannah poured out
her soul before the Lord

00:52:19.510 --> 00:52:21.930
at the tabernacle.

00:52:21.930 --> 00:52:27.170
And after a time of prayer
and speaking with the priests,

00:52:27.170 --> 00:52:30.590
her face was no longer sad.

00:52:30.590 --> 00:52:33.930
She came to the
tabernacle in anguish.

00:52:33.930 --> 00:52:37.220
She left at peace.

00:52:37.220 --> 00:52:39.870
Hannah's story reminds
me of a young woman

00:52:39.870 --> 00:52:45.800
I saw some years ago in the
church I attend near the court.

00:52:45.800 --> 00:52:48.770
As I knelt saying the
rosary after mass,

00:52:48.770 --> 00:52:53.190
I noticed her crying, her
shoulders jerking rhythmically

00:52:53.190 --> 00:52:56.320
as she sobbed heavily.

00:52:56.320 --> 00:53:00.160
We happened to leave the
church at the same time.

00:53:00.160 --> 00:53:05.020
And as we did, I asked
her if she was OK.

00:53:05.020 --> 00:53:08.050
Her face streaked
with mascara, she

00:53:08.050 --> 00:53:14.500
answered in a quiet,
peaceful voice, "I am now."

00:53:14.500 --> 00:53:17.140
Whatever burden that
woman was carrying

00:53:17.140 --> 00:53:21.630
when she entered the church,
she did not leave with it.

00:53:21.630 --> 00:53:24.690
In the words of the
letter to the Hebrews,

00:53:24.690 --> 00:53:28.290
she drew near to
the throne of grace.

00:53:28.290 --> 00:53:32.330
And she did so in
a church building.

00:53:32.330 --> 00:53:34.260
I have no doubt
that many will enter

00:53:34.260 --> 00:53:38.450
here burdened, and like
Hannah, and the young woman,

00:53:38.450 --> 00:53:42.560
leave unburdened and at peace.

00:53:42.560 --> 00:53:46.460
Come to me all who labor
and are heavy laden.

00:53:46.460 --> 00:53:47.415
I will give you rest.

00:53:50.010 --> 00:53:54.780
I humbly offer my own
story that is similar.

00:53:54.780 --> 00:53:58.400
Like Hannah, my life was
changed through prayer

00:53:58.400 --> 00:54:02.010
at a time at a place of worship.

00:54:02.010 --> 00:54:03.960
Although I was raised
Catholic and even

00:54:03.960 --> 00:54:07.050
spent four years
in the seminary,

00:54:07.050 --> 00:54:11.550
in my early adult years, I
became greatly disillusioned

00:54:11.550 --> 00:54:15.780
with the church, and made the
mistake of angrily storming

00:54:15.780 --> 00:54:20.670
away, impetuousness of youth.

00:54:20.670 --> 00:54:24.880
Throughout law school and
the early years of my career,

00:54:24.880 --> 00:54:28.620
I was self-reliant,
so I thought, and gave

00:54:28.620 --> 00:54:32.430
little attention to God.

00:54:32.430 --> 00:54:35.220
But not long after I
joined President Reagan's

00:54:35.220 --> 00:54:38.190
administration, I
was in the midst

00:54:38.190 --> 00:54:43.320
of one of the darkest
periods of my life.

00:54:43.320 --> 00:54:46.500
I was in my 30s,
running a federal agency

00:54:46.500 --> 00:54:50.460
under significant public
scrutiny and criticism.

00:54:50.460 --> 00:54:52.110
I had little money.

00:54:52.110 --> 00:54:53.940
I was raising my young son.

00:54:53.940 --> 00:54:57.930
And I was grieving the loss of
the two most important people

00:54:57.930 --> 00:55:00.570
in my life, my grandparents.

00:55:00.570 --> 00:55:06.140
Life seemed hopeless and felt
like I had nowhere to turn.

00:55:06.140 --> 00:55:08.960
In the midst of this
hardship and grief,

00:55:08.960 --> 00:55:11.420
God drew me back to the church.

00:55:11.420 --> 00:55:14.710
And he used a church
building to do it.

00:55:14.710 --> 00:55:18.900
It was during this period
seemingly bereft of hope

00:55:18.900 --> 00:55:20.880
that I began to
make daily visits

00:55:20.880 --> 00:55:26.100
to local Catholic churches to
pray for wisdom and courage,

00:55:26.100 --> 00:55:29.560
as well as strength
and guidance.

00:55:29.560 --> 00:55:32.500
Unlike the tumultuous
world around me,

00:55:32.500 --> 00:55:37.480
the church building provided
a place of peace, a sanctuary

00:55:37.480 --> 00:55:41.530
from the turmoils of my life.

00:55:41.530 --> 00:55:45.940
Within those walls, with
God's help and grace,

00:55:45.940 --> 00:55:48.700
I was able to
elevate my thoughts

00:55:48.700 --> 00:55:52.810
beyond my circumstances
and self-absorption,

00:55:52.810 --> 00:55:57.190
and set my mind on
things that are above,

00:55:57.190 --> 00:56:01.120
not on things that are on
Earth, as Saint Paul wrote

00:56:01.120 --> 00:56:03.160
in the letter to the Galatians.

00:56:05.830 --> 00:56:09.430
God used these times of
prayer and meditation

00:56:09.430 --> 00:56:13.580
to rekindle the flame
of faith in my life.

00:56:13.580 --> 00:56:15.820
I am a changed man today.

00:56:15.820 --> 00:56:18.580
And God began that
transformation

00:56:18.580 --> 00:56:24.810
in a holy place, a sanctuary,
which like this chapel, where

00:56:24.810 --> 00:56:27.210
I could temporarily--

00:56:27.210 --> 00:56:29.880
a sanctuary much
like this chapel

00:56:29.880 --> 00:56:34.110
where I could temporarily leave
behind the onslaught of life's

00:56:34.110 --> 00:56:39.780
difficulties and bring my
troubles before the Lord.

00:56:39.780 --> 00:56:43.830
God used this renewed
faith to sustain me

00:56:43.830 --> 00:56:47.650
and my wife through my
confirmation hearings.

00:56:47.650 --> 00:56:52.930
And we continue to rely daily
on the grace he gives us.

00:56:52.930 --> 00:56:57.340
But there is nothing unique
about this in our lives.

00:56:57.340 --> 00:57:01.150
For many people,
chapels and churches

00:57:01.150 --> 00:57:06.460
have served as beacons of hope,
physical reminders of our need

00:57:06.460 --> 00:57:09.160
for God and his grace.

00:57:09.160 --> 00:57:12.540
And the presence of a
chapel on a college campus

00:57:12.540 --> 00:57:14.990
is particularly important.

00:57:14.990 --> 00:57:19.930
In fact, in this age
of popular iconoclasm,

00:57:19.930 --> 00:57:25.630
building a chapel on a college
campus is all but verboten.

00:57:25.630 --> 00:57:29.020
The college years
require young people

00:57:29.020 --> 00:57:34.030
to make decisions that will
affect the rest of their lives.

00:57:34.030 --> 00:57:38.270
They are exposed to new
ideas, new relationships,

00:57:38.270 --> 00:57:42.670
new distractions,
and new temptations.

00:57:42.670 --> 00:57:44.380
They need a place
where they can go

00:57:44.380 --> 00:57:50.620
to be relieved of their troubles
and get their bearing as so

00:57:50.620 --> 00:57:54.180
much comes at them so fast.

00:57:54.180 --> 00:57:57.390
By building this chapel,
Hillsdale College

00:57:57.390 --> 00:58:00.180
has provided that
space where students

00:58:00.180 --> 00:58:03.300
can come to discern
God's calling,

00:58:03.300 --> 00:58:06.660
to pray through difficult
times, and to praise

00:58:06.660 --> 00:58:09.910
God for his faithfulness.

00:58:09.910 --> 00:58:15.090
In short, Hillsdale College
has recognized the importance

00:58:15.090 --> 00:58:20.250
of equipping students not
only intellectually, but also

00:58:20.250 --> 00:58:24.720
spiritually for the many
challenges of life in college

00:58:24.720 --> 00:58:25.450
and beyond.

00:58:28.220 --> 00:58:31.920
Although a chapel is a
place for many activities,

00:58:31.920 --> 00:58:35.840
it also serves as a statement
about the importance

00:58:35.840 --> 00:58:38.420
of those activities.

00:58:38.420 --> 00:58:45.010
The construction of a
college chapel in particular

00:58:45.010 --> 00:58:49.360
is a public declaration
that faith and reason

00:58:49.360 --> 00:58:52.480
are mutually reinforcing.

00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:56.920
And in 2019, the
construction of a chapel

00:58:56.920 --> 00:59:01.960
is a bold act of leadership at
a crucial time in our nation's

00:59:01.960 --> 00:59:04.150
history.

00:59:04.150 --> 00:59:07.000
So I would like to
briefly underscore

00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:10.810
the broader significance
of the decision

00:59:10.810 --> 00:59:14.440
that Hillsdale College has
made in building Christ Chapel.

00:59:17.200 --> 00:59:22.420
Beginning in the early 1900s,
many elite private colleges

00:59:22.420 --> 00:59:25.930
and universities began
to face questions

00:59:25.930 --> 00:59:29.890
about the continuing relevance
of religious instruction

00:59:29.890 --> 00:59:30.430
on campus.

00:59:33.000 --> 00:59:35.870
These questions would have
surprised the founders

00:59:35.870 --> 00:59:39.260
of those schools, many
of which were created

00:59:39.260 --> 00:59:43.190
in part for the expressed
purpose of providing

00:59:43.190 --> 00:59:45.890
religious instruction.

00:59:45.890 --> 00:59:48.530
But as time went on
and schools moved away

00:59:48.530 --> 00:59:51.530
from their religious
roots, the relevance

00:59:51.530 --> 00:59:56.480
of religion to higher education
was increasingly questioned.

00:59:56.480 --> 00:59:59.450
And campus chapels
in particular came

00:59:59.450 --> 01:00:04.450
to be viewed as relics
of a bygone era.

01:00:04.450 --> 01:00:07.780
With the completion
of Christ Chapel,

01:00:07.780 --> 01:00:12.760
Hillsdale College has staked
out its position in this debate.

01:00:12.760 --> 01:00:17.610
And its decision serves as
an example for all of us.

01:00:17.610 --> 01:00:22.380
The construction of so
grand a chapel in 2019

01:00:22.380 --> 01:00:27.700
does not happen by accident
or as an afterthought.

01:00:27.700 --> 01:00:31.300
Christ Chapel reflects
the college's conviction

01:00:31.300 --> 01:00:34.420
that a vibrant
intellectual environment

01:00:34.420 --> 01:00:39.820
and a strong democratic society
are fostered, not hindered,

01:00:39.820 --> 01:00:43.400
by a recognition of the divine.

01:00:43.400 --> 01:00:47.960
Hillsdale College affirms
with the writer of Proverbs

01:00:47.960 --> 01:00:52.250
that "the fear of the Lord
is the beginning of wisdom

01:00:52.250 --> 01:00:56.430
and the knowledge of the
Holy One is insight."

01:00:56.430 --> 01:00:59.670
By constructing this
chapel, the college

01:00:59.670 --> 01:01:03.660
upholds the continued importance
of its Christian roots,

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:08.280
even as it respects the rights
of each person to worship God

01:01:08.280 --> 01:01:12.930
according to the dictates
of his own conscience.

01:01:12.930 --> 01:01:15.810
Our country was
founded on the view

01:01:15.810 --> 01:01:19.530
that a correct understanding
of the nature of God

01:01:19.530 --> 01:01:22.830
and the human person is
critical to preserving

01:01:22.830 --> 01:01:26.370
the liberty that we so enjoy.

01:01:26.370 --> 01:01:29.870
John Adams wrote,
"Our constitution

01:01:29.870 --> 01:01:33.860
was made only for a moral
and religious people.

01:01:33.860 --> 01:01:38.840
It is wholly inadequate to
the government of any other."

01:01:38.840 --> 01:01:43.190
He recognized that the
preservation of liberty

01:01:43.190 --> 01:01:45.620
is not guaranteed.

01:01:45.620 --> 01:01:50.150
Without the guardrails supplied
by religious conviction,

01:01:50.150 --> 01:01:55.610
popular sovereignty can
devolve into mob rule, unmoored

01:01:55.610 --> 01:01:59.840
from any conception
of objective truth.

01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:02.990
As I think about our
political culture today,

01:02:02.990 --> 01:02:06.910
I am reminded of Ronald
Reagan's warning,

01:02:06.910 --> 01:02:10.450
that freedom is never more
than one generation away

01:02:10.450 --> 01:02:12.980
from extinction.

01:02:12.980 --> 01:02:16.810
We didn't pass it to our
children in the bloodstream.

01:02:16.810 --> 01:02:21.940
The only way they can inherit
the freedom we have known

01:02:21.940 --> 01:02:26.320
is if we fight for it, protect
it, defend it, and then

01:02:26.320 --> 01:02:30.660
hand it to them to do the same.

01:02:30.660 --> 01:02:34.710
Each generation is
responsible to both itself

01:02:34.710 --> 01:02:39.150
and to succeeding generations
for preserving and promoting

01:02:39.150 --> 01:02:41.940
the blessings of liberty.

01:02:41.940 --> 01:02:45.480
Faith in God, more
than anything else,

01:02:45.480 --> 01:02:49.080
fuels the strength of
character and self-discipline

01:02:49.080 --> 01:02:54.210
necessary to ably discharge
that responsibility.

01:02:54.210 --> 01:02:59.460
That is why I am so encouraged
by the construction of Christ

01:02:59.460 --> 01:03:01.190
Chapel.

01:03:01.190 --> 01:03:05.420
Hillsdale College's
Articles of Association

01:03:05.420 --> 01:03:09.410
affirm that
"inestimable blessings

01:03:09.410 --> 01:03:13.340
flow from the prevalence of
civil and religious liberty

01:03:13.340 --> 01:03:17.090
and intelligent
piety in the land."

01:03:17.090 --> 01:03:18.950
The college was
founded on the belief

01:03:18.950 --> 01:03:21.980
that the diffusion
of sound blending

01:03:21.980 --> 01:03:25.970
is essential to the
perpetuity of these blessings.

01:03:25.970 --> 01:03:31.940
Thus, Hillsdale College was
founded on the understanding

01:03:31.940 --> 01:03:37.010
that the battle to preserve and
promote freedom in our country

01:03:37.010 --> 01:03:41.780
will be waged in the hearts
and minds of the people.

01:03:41.780 --> 01:03:44.510
Rather than shrinking
from the battle,

01:03:44.510 --> 01:03:47.330
Hillsdale is rising
to the occasion

01:03:47.330 --> 01:03:51.440
by investing in the intellectual
and spiritual development

01:03:51.440 --> 01:03:56.450
of its students so they can
provide God-honoring leadership

01:03:56.450 --> 01:03:59.150
in our country.

01:03:59.150 --> 01:04:01.480
Let it be said of
them what was said

01:04:01.480 --> 01:04:05.650
of David, that he served
the counsel of God

01:04:05.650 --> 01:04:07.050
in his own generation.

01:04:10.320 --> 01:04:13.390
Students, faculty,
administrators,

01:04:13.390 --> 01:04:16.540
and friends of Hillsdale,
let this chapel

01:04:16.540 --> 01:04:19.160
be more than just an
impressive building.

01:04:24.740 --> 01:04:27.020
Let it be a place
where people enter

01:04:27.020 --> 01:04:30.190
the presence of a majestic God.

01:04:30.190 --> 01:04:34.420
Let it be a house of worship,
of prayer, of meditation,

01:04:34.420 --> 01:04:37.450
and of celebration before God.

01:04:37.450 --> 01:04:41.260
Let it be a haven of
rest for the weary,

01:04:41.260 --> 01:04:44.080
a place of healing
for the wounded,

01:04:44.080 --> 01:04:48.010
a place of comfort for the
grieving, and a source of hope

01:04:48.010 --> 01:04:52.000
for the despairing
and forgotten.

01:04:52.000 --> 01:04:55.300
Let it point to a day
when the dwelling of God

01:04:55.300 --> 01:04:59.560
will be with men, when
God himself will wipe away

01:04:59.560 --> 01:05:02.920
every tear and mend every wound.

01:05:02.920 --> 01:05:06.460
Let it be a place where
tomorrow's leaders discern

01:05:06.460 --> 01:05:10.870
their callings and grow
firm in their convictions.

01:05:10.870 --> 01:05:16.120
Let it stand as a bold
declaration to a watching world

01:05:16.120 --> 01:05:18.520
that faith and
learning are rightly

01:05:18.520 --> 01:05:21.790
understood as
complements and that both

01:05:21.790 --> 01:05:24.460
are essential to
the preservation

01:05:24.460 --> 01:05:27.010
of the blessings of liberty.

01:05:27.010 --> 01:05:31.060
Above all, let this
chapel equip and inspire

01:05:31.060 --> 01:05:35.740
us to honor God in
whatever he calls us to do.

01:05:35.740 --> 01:05:38.920
For as Saint Paul wrote in
the letter to the Romans,

01:05:38.920 --> 01:05:43.990
"From him and through him
and to him are all things.

01:05:43.990 --> 01:05:47.380
To him be the glory
forever, Amen."

01:05:47.380 --> 01:05:49.120
May God bless each of you.

01:05:49.120 --> 01:05:51.010
May God bless Hillsdale.

01:05:51.010 --> 01:05:54.220
And may God bless this
wonderful country.

01:05:54.220 --> 01:05:55.420
Thank you.

01:05:55.420 --> 01:05:57.270
[APPLAUSE]

